/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#customization","content":"Compose related `Collapsible` sections inside Accordion. Give each section a stable, unique `id`.\nSee Collapsible for the section anatomy, panel content, and trigger styling."},"52":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-28","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#customization","content":"Use `defaultExpandedKeys` for initial expansion, or `expandedKeys` with `onExpandedChange` for\ncontrolled state. Keys must match the section IDs; the callback receives a `Set` of expanded keys.\nBy default, only one section can stay open. Set `allowsMultipleExpanded` to keep several open.\nBoth behaviors are shown in the examples."},"53":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-29","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#customization","content":"Use `className` and `style` to customize the group container. `data-disabled` reflects the group's\ndisabled state. Customize individual headings, triggers, and panels on the composed Collapsible sections."},"54":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-30","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#accessibility","content":"Each section provides its own heading and button-to-panel relationship. Choose heading levels that\nfit the page hierarchy. The Collapsible accessibility guidance\ncovers keyboard interaction, focus, and status icons."},"55":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-31","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#accessibility","content":"To identify the whole accordion as a named group, provide `role=\"group\"` together with `aria-label`\nor `aria-labelledby`. Setting `isDisabled` on Accordion disables every section's trigger."},"56":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-32","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#best-practices","content":"Group related sections and keep essential information visible outside the accordion."},"57":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-33","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#best-practices","content":"Use multiple expansion when users need to compare information across sections."},"58":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-34","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#best-practices","content":"Keep item IDs stable when reordering or filtering data."},"59":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-35","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#best-practices","content":"Manage expansion on Accordion when sections belong to a group."},"60":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-36","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#best-practices","content":"Keep form validation and step progression in application logic."},"61":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-37","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#controlled-state-not-updating","content":"Update `expandedKeys` from `onExpandedChange` and make sure the keys match the item IDs.\nChanging `defaultExpandedKeys` after mounting does not control expansion."},"62":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-38","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#sections-close-when-another-opens","content":"Enable `allowsMultipleExpanded` when several sections should remain open together.\nFor a single independent section, use Collapsible without an Accordion."},"63":{"id":"/docs/components/alert","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"page","content":"Alert","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert"},"64":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-0","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert","content":"In-page alerts are non-intrusive notifications within a webpage, providing users with timely information or feedback without disrupting their experience."},"65":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-1","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#installation","content":"Installation"},"66":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-2","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#examples","content":"Examples"},"67":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-3","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#default","content":"Default"},"68":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-4","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#emphasis-variants","content":"Emphasis Variants"},"69":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-5","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#dismissible","content":"Dismissible"},"70":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-6","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#with-action","content":"With Action"},"71":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-7","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"72":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-8","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#keyboard","content":"Keyboard"},"73":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-9","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#screen-readers","content":"Screen readers"},"74":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-10","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#dismiss-button-label","content":"Dismiss button label"},"75":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-11","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"76":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-12","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#props","content":"Props"},"77":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-13","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#alert","content":"Alert"},"78":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-14","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#default","content":"A minimal alert with a title and body text."},"79":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-15","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#emphasis-variants","content":"All 7 emphasis categories. Each variant carries a distinct visual accent and semantic icon so the type of message is never communicated by color alone."},"80":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-16","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#dismissible","content":"When an `onClose` callback is provided, a dismiss button is rendered. The component does not manage its own visibility — the parent is responsible for unmounting or hiding the alert when `onClose` fires."},"81":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-17","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#with-action","content":"Pass a `Button` to the `actions` slot to give the user a clear path to resolve the alert."},"82":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-18","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#keyboard","content":"Key"},"83":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-19","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#keyboard","content":"Description"},"84":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-20","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#keyboard","content":"`Tab`"},"85":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-21","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#keyboard","content":"Moves focus to the dismiss button or action button"},"86":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-22","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#keyboard","content":"`Space` / `Enter`"},"87":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-23","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#keyboard","content":"Activates the focused button"},"88":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-24","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#screen-readers","content":"The alert container uses `role=\"alert\"`, which creates an ARIA live region. When an alert is rendered or its content changes, screen readers announce the message automatically — the user does not need to navigate to the alert to hear it."},"89":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-25","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#dismiss-button-label","content":"The dismiss button defaults to `aria-label=\"Close\"`. Override it via `ariaLabels={{ close: '...' }}` to provide more specific context for screen readers (e.g. `\"Dismiss payment warning\"`). This is especially useful when multiple alerts are visible at the same time."},"90":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-26","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#best-practices","content":"Write alert content from the user's perspective: describe what happened and what they can do next, not the underlying technical error."},"91":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-27","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#best-practices","content":"Use `critical` only when the user truly cannot continue without resolving the issue. Overusing it reduces its impact."},"92":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-28","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#best-practices","content":"Always provide a `title` when the alert includes a dismiss button — it improves the reading experience for screen reader users."},"93":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-29","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#best-practices","content":"When using `actions`, prefer `secondary` or `tertiary` Button variants. Avoid placing a primary action inside an alert."},"94":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-30","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#best-practices","content":"Do not stack multiple alerts of the same emphasis; consolidate the message into a single alert."},"95":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","type":"page","content":"Avatar","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/avatar"},"96":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-0","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/avatar","content":"A visual representation of a user or entity, shown as a photo or a monogram of their initials."},"97":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-1","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/avatar#features","content":"Features"},"98":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-2","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/avatar#installation","content":"Installation"},"99":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-3","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/avatar#examples","content":"Examples"},"100":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-4","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/avatar#default","content":"Default"},"101":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-5","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","type":"heading","tags